CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu
 /rsvp_boot?id=1632412\n\nDescription:\nThis year marks the 27th annual Tra
 nsgender Day of Remembrance (TDOR). Founded formally in 1999 by Gwendolyn 
 Ann Smith in honor of Rita Hester\, a transgender woman who was murdered i
 n Allston\, Massachusetts\, this day is dedicated to the transgender peopl
 e whose lives have been lost due to transphobia and anti-trans violence.\n
 As the actual TDOR (November 20th) falls outside the term\, we will host a
  flag display and community gathering on Wednesday\, November 4th to honor
  and recognize those lost and increase awareness while respecting the need
 s of students at the end of the term.\nRSVP for location of community gath
 ering at dartgo.org/qsa\nFood Provided\n\nSponsor / organizer: Office of P
 luralism and Leadership\n\nSource: Dartmouth Groups\n\nWhy this was includ
 ed: explicit food-service wording\; food keyword near service context\n\nF
 ood availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify details befo
 re attending.
